        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm looking at the dhatu घृणुँ from tanadi gana, meaning दीप्तौ (to shine). I'm checking the accent mark on it to determine if it's svarita or anudatta based on the diacritic notation.\n\nSince this root is marked स्वरितेत्, it's ubhayapadi, and in the tanadi group it takes the उ vikarana. Working through the parasmaipada lat first person singular, I get घृणोमि through guna of the उ augment, confirming the vikarana is ardhadhatuka since it's not a शित् affix.\n\nRight, there's a vartika \"उप्रत्यये लघूपधगुणो वा\" allowing optional guna before this उ-pratyaya, giving क्षिणोति/क्षेणोति and similarly तृणोति/तर्णोति, घृणोति/घर्णोति — either is valid, so I'll settle on one form for घृ. For आत्मनेपद, since the penultimate is a single consonant, the उ-lopa before म्/व् is optional: घृणुवे or घृण्वे.\n\nFor परस्मैपद मि, guna applies first blocking the optional lopa (which only operates on कित्/ङित् forms), so the form is simply घृणोमि — that's my final answer.\n\n",
